import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="groundwaterwatch — Europe's hidden drought, mapped weekly">
  <h1>Europe's hidden drought</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    NASA's GRACE-FO satellites have been measuring how much water sits beneath
    Europe's surface for 23 years. The picture they paint of Romania and
    Hungary right now is the driest it has ever been at this time of year —
    drier than 98% of weeks in the last three quarters of a century.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is a public dashboard, updated weekly. We pull the same data NASA
    publishes and break it down by NUTS-2 region so you can see where the
    aquifer collapse is sharpest. v1 covers Romania and Hungary. Other
    countries follow.
  </p>

  <h2>Pick a country</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/ro/">Romania</a> — 8 NUTS-2 regions</li>
    <li><a href="/hu/">Hungary</a> — 8 NUTS-2 regions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to read the percentile</h2>
  <p>
    Every cell on the map and every region table reports a
    <strong>groundwater percentile</strong> against a 75-year baseline
    (1948–2014). A value of 2 means: only in 2% of historical weeks at this
    time of year was the water table this depleted or worse.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    Methodology, source data, and what this dashboard does <em>not</em> measure
    are documented on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. Please
    read it before quoting the numbers.
  </div>
</Base>
